<title>USA: FOB GULF GRAIN - SOY OFFERS MOSTLY UP, CORN SLIPS.</title>
<headline>FOB GULF GRAIN - SOY OFFERS MOSTLY UP, CORN SLIPS.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. FOB Gulf soybean offers were mostly higher Wednesday, underpinned partly by increased export demand, while corn values slipped, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;People were trying to short-cover and there are not a lot of beans to buy,&quot; one U.S. soybean exporter said.</p>
<p>Grain traders noted market talk that soybeans were needed to meet export commitments on the U.S. Great Lakes and the Gulf of Mexico but that supplies of old-crop soybeans were not adequate.  </p>
